Package: normpipe
Type: Package
Title: Population-Referenced Norms with Two Layers of Uncertainty for Any Questionnaire
Version: 0.2.3
Authors@R: c(
    person("Johannes", "Zimmermann", email = "jz@uni-kassel.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Derives norm tables for self-report questionnaires from a
    weighted reference sample or from published frequency tables. An
    instrument is described in a configuration file (items with their
    response categories and values, versions and scales, reporting cells);
    the pipeline then produces weighted percentile and T norms per reporting
    cell with credible bands from a Bayesian bootstrap under a Dirichlet
    prior over the attainable scores, continuous-age kernel norms,
    score-conditional and integrated intervals for the individual from
    calibrated graded response and bifactor models, and several export
    formats. An optional transfer module projects scales that the reference
    sample did not answer from bridge items, using donor samples and Bayesian
    distributional regression.
